11.0.0, eighth upload — loop it, layer it, record without setting up

What is new since 10010. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and, where a test
target reaches it, tests; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- The song loops. The Loop button in the transport (on by default) repeats the song from bar 1
  at its last bar, sample-exact and the same at every buffer size; switching it off lets the
  song run on.
- Overdub: a MIDI take that runs through the loop's end keeps recording into the same take on
  the next pass, so a second layer adds to the first. An audio take suspends the loop while it
  records and gives it back when it ends.
- Record without setting up: with no track armed, Record arms the track the keys play and
  records it.
- A plugin's settings are taken only from the plugin the song names. During a swap the old unit
  can no longer write its settings into the new one, and a failed capture keeps the last good
  state.
- Groundwork for the body (no screen or sensor yet): pulse conditioning, pulse period, HRV
  (RMSSD, SDNN, pNN50), interval hygiene and coherence are in the DSP package with their tests.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10010), seventh upload — play it with the phone alone (keys and pads on the screen, Four Tracks on first launch, store and plugin-window repairs). Before that: 11.0.0 (10009), sixth upload — the app survives what a device does to it. 10008, fifth upload — the plugin purchase in the App Group group.com.echoelmusic.shared. Before that: 10007, 10006, 10005, 10004 (the first Echoel Studio build). group.com.echoelmusic (the import of earlier songs) is still not requested (F17): until it is, the import finds nothing.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Open Four Tracks, press Play: at the end of the song it starts again at bar 1 without a gap
   or click. Tap Loop off: it plays on past the end.
2. With nothing armed, press Record and play four notes on the screen keys: Record works without
   arming, and the take lands on the Keys track.
3. Keep recording through two loop passes, playing different notes each pass: after Stop, both
   layers play back, and no note is doubled.
4. Record a short take on a track with a microphone or interface input: the loop pauses during
   the take and is back on after Stop.
5. Load a third-party plugin on a track, change a knob, swap the plugin for another one, save,
   reopen the song: the new plugin opens with its own settings, not the old one's.
